    "body": "## Summary\n- add Flyway V46 persistence for the Stripe platform-to-connected transfer reference\n- register live `stripe-connect` dispatch only behind a separate `PAYOUT_STRIPE_CONNECT_DISPATCH_ENABLED` kill switch\n- perform a fresh recipient readiness check and force manual payout scheduling before any money movement\n- use separate stable idempotency keys for platform transfer, connected-account payout and failure reversal\n- persist/validate the transfer before creating the connected-account bank payout so retries cannot transfer funds twice\n- settle terminal Stripe Connect payouts only from signed webhook events\n- validate payout id, user id, connected account, amount, currency and transfer metadata before settlement\n- on failed/canceled bank payout, reverse the original transfer back to the platform before allowing `PAYOUT_RESTORE`\n- extend payout smoke to validate V46 while keeping sandbox and both Connect kill switches disabled\n- document live operational and ledger invariants\n\n## Safety / ledger invariants\n- `PAYOUT_RESERVE` remains the only wallet debit when the payout request is accepted\n- Stripe payout creation always maps to `SUBMITTED`, never directly to `PAID`\n- `payout.paid` creates no second wallet debit\n- `payout.failed` cannot restore wallet funds until the matching platform transfer has been safely recovered\n- ambiguous provider failures retain the wallet reservation; they never mint spendable balance\n- disabling live dispatch does not disable signed settlement handling for payouts already in flight\n- onboarding alone cannot enable money movement\n\n## Validation\nMerge only after every latest-head API, web, runtime, payout and payment check has completed successfully.",
